    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class; the other two files are the base harness and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nTo make owner creation return `displayName` as `LastName, FirstName`, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `displayName` field (with getter/setter) that gets serialized in the JSON responses for both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 annotated `toOwnerDto(Owner)` with a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes the field from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nThis composes the value directly from the persisted `lastName`/`firstName`, matching the required `\"LastName, FirstName\"` format exactly. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
